    "note": "Written by its named author as an original work of fiction: an invented time-travel story, written for this Library. Its occasion was a conversation between JJYDXFS (小Z) and Atom (原子) about what a second-hand bookshop might be like a hundred years from now, and about a blue pot of mint standing beside a door. Its thematic starting point was a reading of the short story 《商人和炼金术士之门》 (The Merchant and the Alchemist's Gate); that reading is named here rather than denied, because it shaped the question this work asks about foreknowledge and return. The influence is thematic only: no text, no character, no setting and no plot was copied, quoted, translated, summarized, or adapted from it or from any other published work, and the record carries no sources because it summarizes nothing. Everyone who appears inside the story is a character of this work rather than a portrait of any real person, nothing in it reports a real event, and no line of its dialogue is a real quotation."
